Consider the task of robust language identification in the limit with the set machines as DPDAs, then
• There is an algorithm that guarantees to succeed in the diminishing error rate regime;
• Robust language identification is impossible in the constant error rate regime, for any constant α > 0.

Consider the task of robust language identification in the limit with the set machines as Turing machines, then
• There is an algorithm that guarantees to succeed when the number of errors is finite;
• Robust language identification is impossible even in the diminishing error regime.
